From f310672f09b15475d102b0b66474922f253fec33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harvester57 <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:59:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [e-acsl] type all sibling subterms and quantifier goals after
 Not_yet

In Typing (plugins/e-acsl/src/analyses/typing.ml), composite predicates
such as Pand/Prel and Tapp already ensure all children are typed even
when an earlier child raises Error.Not_yet, because Labels.preprocess
registers \at/\old subterms in every branch for Translate_ats.for_stmt
and Loops.mk_nested_loops translates quantifier goals before bounds.

Other composite cases still short-circuited on the first Error.Not_yet
(either when computing a typing context or when typing children
sequentially):
- Pforall/Pexists and type_bound_variables skipped remaining guards and
  the quantifier goal (causing "typing was not performed" on quantifiers
  with an unsupported bound, and on stpncpy's dest_nul_padded
  postcondition);
- TBinOp skipped the second operand (causing "typing was not performed
  on construct 1" when Translate_ats pre-translated \old(src)'s
  alignment RTE guard in strlcat's bounded_result postcondition);
- the same pattern affected TUnOp, TCast, Tif, Trange, Tlet, Pif, Plet,
  Papp, Pseparated, and Paligned.

Use shared do_both, do_all, and with_opt_ctx helpers so every sibling
subterm, bound, and quantifier goal is typed before re-raising the first
typing/unsupported error.

New test: plugins/e-acsl/tests/constructs/typing_unsupported_sibling.c.
---
 plugins/e-acsl/src/analyses/typing.ml         |  215 +--
 .../oracle/gen_typing_unsupported_sibling.0.c | 1161 +++++++++++++++++
 .../typing_unsupported_sibling.0.res.oracle   |  119 ++
 .../constructs/typing_unsupported_sibling.c   |   28 +
 4 files changed, 1444 insertions(+), 79 deletions(-)
